menu "PSU-EXT configuration"

menu "Calibration"

config PSUEXT_CAL_REQUIRE_MIN_POINTS_PER_PGA
    bool "Require a minimum number of points per PGA range"
    default y
    help
        Require each configured ADS1115 PGA range to have the configured
        minimum number of calibration points before a table can be committed.
        Disable this to allow a valid table with any represented ranges; the
        firmware-wide minimum of two table points still applies.

config PSUEXT_CAL_MIN_POINTS_PER_PGA
    int "Minimum calibration points per PGA range"
    depends on PSUEXT_CAL_REQUIRE_MIN_POINTS_PER_PGA
    range 2 8
    default 2
    help
        Number of strictly increasing calibration points required for
        every configured ADS1115 PGA range when committing a calibration
        table. The upper bound of eight keeps a valid table possible within
        the firmware's 32-point limit and four possible PGA ranges.

endmenu

endmenu
